<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vigdís Finnbogadóttir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1930</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vigdís Finnbogadóttir was president of Iceland from 1980 to 1996, the world's first woman elected head of state in a democratic national election. A teacher and director of the Reykjavík <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a> Company before her election, she was re-elected three times. As president she promoted the Icelandic language, culture and reforestation, and later became an international advocate for linguistic diversity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vigdis-finnbogadottir.jpg" alt="Vigdís Finnbogadóttir" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob Croes for Anefo · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vigdis_Finnbogadottir_(1985).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
